  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Find two fractions between $\\frac{5}{8}$ and $\\frac{2}{3}$ so that the gaps between all four numbers are the same.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{23}{36},\\ \\frac{47}{72}$.\n\nRewrite the endpoints with denominator $72$; the four numerators are consecutive.",
      "worked": "Use equivalent fractions with a common denominator:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5}{8}&=\\frac{45}{72}\\\\\\frac{2}{3}&=\\frac{48}{72}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe three equal gaps are each $\\frac{1}{72}$. The two interior fractions are\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{46}{72}&=\\frac{23}{36}\\\\\\frac{47}{72}&=\\frac{47}{72}.\\end{align*}$$\nCheck:\n$$\\frac{46}{72}-\\frac{45}{72}=\\frac{47}{72}-\\frac{46}{72}=\\frac{48}{72}-\\frac{47}{72}=\\frac{1}{72}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 74
  },
